# "self" and "me": get_char_room_vis's own special case (handler.c:1068),
# whose whole comment in the C is `/* JE 7/18/94 :-) :-) */`. It sits after
# get_number and before both the zero-count branch and CAN_SEE, so the count
# is read and ignored and a blind character can still name themselves.
Parityone
y
swordfish
swordfish
m
w

1
goto 3001
look self
look me
look 2.self
look 0.me
kill self
hit self
kill me
kill Parityone
# `0.<name>` means "a player with this name", which is the branch just below
# the self one. `look` cannot reach it -- generic_find gives up on a zero
# count before searching anything -- but `hit` calls get_char_vis directly and
# does, so naming yourself this way lands on do_hit's own self-refusal.
look 0.parityone
hit 0.parityone
hit 0.nobody
# A word that is not "self" and names nobody, for the refusal beside it.
kill nobody
look nobody
quit
